# Ex commands after :.

=== :s replaces the first match on the line
text:
|a a a
keys: :s/a/b/<CR>
want:
|b a a

=== :s with g replaces all
text:
|a a a
keys: :s/a/b/g<CR>
want:
|b b b

=== :%s on every line
text:
|foo 1
foo 2
bar foo
keys: :%s/foo/x/<CR>
want:
x 1
x 2
|bar x

=== groups and & in the replacement
text:
|john smith
keys: :s/\(\w\+\) \(\w\+\)/\2, \1 (&)/<CR>
want:
|smith, john (john smith)

=== case modifiers
text:
|hello world
keys: :s/\w\+/\u&/g<CR>
want:
|Hello World

=== \r inserts a line break
text:
|a,b
keys: :s/,/\r/<CR>
want:
a
|b

=== a range of lines
text:
|x
x
x
x
keys: :2,3s/x/y/<CR>
want:
x
y
|y
x

=== the visual lines as the range
text:
|a
a
a
keys: Vj:s/a/b/<CR>
want:
b
|b
a

=== a line number moves there
text:
|one
  two
three
keys: :2<CR>
want:
one
  |two
three

=== :d deletes lines
text:
|1
2
3
keys: :2,3d<CR>
want:
|1

=== an unknown command is an error
text:
|x
keys: :nosuch<CR>
want:
|x
error: yes

=== :s without a match is an error
text:
|x
keys: :s/zzz/y/<CR>
want:
|x
error: yes

=== :noh and :set keep the text
text:
|x
keys: :set ic<CR>:noh<CR>
want:
|x

=== ignorecase set by :set
text:
|a FOO
keys: :set ic<CR>/foo<CR>
want:
a |FOO

=== Esc cancels the command line
text:
|abc
keys: :s/a/b/<Esc>
want:
|abc
mode: vim/normal

=== :w writes the file
text:
|abc
keys: xx:w<CR>
want:
|c
